  "summary": "Oak Park's Citizen Police Oversight Committee, in its semi-annual report, said the police department has refused to share data on case outcomes from Flock ALPR searches, making it impossible to evaluate the system's effectiveness. The committee formally recommended the village board require OPPD to share detailed search and outcome data, noting only two stops resulted from Flock data in the second half of 2024 despite ~2.1 searches per day.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Despite repeated requests by CPOC for evidence of 'successful investigative outcomes' to illustrate the value of Flock Safety ALPR for this use, OPPD remains unwilling to provide such data",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "there is no evidence whatsoever that Flock Safety ALPRs have played a meaningful role in any Oak Park crime investigation since their installation in 2022",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "Evaluating search justifications, false positives, and case outcomes enables CPOC to determine whether ALPR searches lead to lawful, unbiased, and effective enforcement actions",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    }
  ],
